IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clatas-dates`
IMPORT `clatas-common`
IMPORT `clatas-liability`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (Tas) -- baseline-2026-11: cases for clatas-liability.l4 (Parts 4, 6, 8, 8A, 8B, 9, 9A, 10,
-- 10A, 10B). Edges: each s 3B class a Part keeps or loses; each start date; each exception to each protection.
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Cases -- liability`

§§ `Short names`

`ordinary` MEANS `an ordinary claim: none of the s 3B exclusions`
`child abuse` MEANS `an intentional act that is child abuse within s 49J(3) (s 3B(1A))`
`intentional` MEANS `another intentional act done with intent to cause injury or death, or sexual assault or other sexual misconduct (s 3B(1)(a))`
`motor` MEANS `an injury Part III of the Motor Accidents (Liabilities and Compensation) Act 1973 applies to (s 3B(2))`
`work injury` MEANS `an injury Division 2 of Part X of the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 applies to (s 3B(3))`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`2015` MEANS d 1 6 2015

§§ `s 7 -- apologies`

`apology` MEANS `Can the apology be used as evidence of fault`
#ASSERT apology `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT apology `ordinary` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT apology `ordinary` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT apology `ordinary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3B(2): Part 4 is not kept for a Part III motor accident injury.
#ASSERT apology `motor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7AB: proceedings begun before the 2024 Act's Royal Assent are left to s 7 as it then stood (not deposited).
#ASSERT apology `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT apology `ordinary` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 11, 13 -- breach and causation`

`breach` MEANS `Do breach and causation stand in my way`
#ASSERT breach `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ss 11 and 13 do not stand in the way of my claim`
#ASSERT breach `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no breach: the risk was not foreseeable (s 11(1)(a))`
#ASSERT breach `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no breach: the risk was insignificant (s 11(1)(b))`
#ASSERT breach `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no breach: a reasonable person would not have taken precautions (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT breach `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no causation: the breach was not a necessary element of the harm (s 13(1)(a))`
#ASSERT breach `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no causation: the harm is outside the scope of liability (s 13(1)(b))`
#ASSERT breach `motor` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ss 11 and 13 do not stand in the way of my claim`
#ASSERT breach `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Part 6 does not apply to my claim`
#ASSERT breach `intentional` `2015` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Part 6 does not apply to my claim`

§§ `ss 16, 17 -- obvious risks`

`aware` MEANS `Am I taken to have known of the risk`
#ASSERT aware `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT aware `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT aware `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT aware `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; obvious; I asked; written law; professional (not medical); risk from their service to me.
`warn` MEANS `Did the defendant owe me a duty to warn of an obvious risk`
#ASSERT warn `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT warn `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warn `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warn `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A professional, but the risk is not of death or injury from the service: s 17(1) still bites.
#ASSERT warn `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT warn `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 20 -- dangerous recreational activities`

`recreation` MEANS `Can I hold the defendant liable for a dangerous recreational activity`
#ASSERT recreation `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT recreation `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT recreation `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT recreation `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3B(2): Division 5 is not kept for a Part III motor accident injury.
#ASSERT recreation `motor` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 21, 22 -- professional negligence`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; acted promptly for serious risk; could not respond; no time to contact; not given what a
-- reasonable person would need; not given what I wanted.
`doctor` MEANS `Did my doctor breach the duty to warn`
#ASSERT doctor `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT doctor `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT doctor `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21(2): an emergency, all three limbs.
#ASSERT doctor `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Two limbs only: s 21 still applies.
#ASSERT doctor `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT doctor `motor` `2015` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

`peers` MEANS `Can my professional be found in breach despite peer opinion`
#ASSERT peers `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT peers `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT peers `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22(5): a warning case.
#ASSERT peers `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT peers `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT peers `motor` `2015` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 8 -- mental harm`

`family` MEANS `Am I a close member of the victim's family`
#ASSERT family `parent, or another person with parental responsibility for the victim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT family `husband, wife or de facto spouse (the last to qualify, if more than one)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT family `an earlier husband, wife or de facto spouse, where a later one also qualifies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT family `child or stepchild, or a person for whom the victim has parental responsibility` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT family `brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, stepbrother or stepsister` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT family `another relationship, or none` EQUALS JUST FALSE

`saw it` MEANS `the victim being killed, injured or put in peril`
`aftermath` MEANS `the immediate aftermath of the victim being killed or injured`
`peril aftermath` MEANS `the immediate aftermath of the victim being put in peril, without being killed or injured`
`not there` MEANS `nothing at the scene`
`stranger` MEANS `another relationship, or none`
`parent` MEANS `parent, or another person with parental responsibility for the victim`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; psychiatric illness; witnessed; relationship; normal fortitude foreseeable.
`shock` MEANS `Can I recover for pure mental harm from shock`
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` `2015` TRUE `saw it` `stranger` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` `2015` TRUE `aftermath` `stranger` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` `2015` TRUE `not there` `parent` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The aftermath of mere peril does not count (s 32(2)(a)).
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` `2015` TRUE `peril aftermath` `stranger` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` `2015` TRUE `not there` `stranger` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33: not a recognised psychiatric illness.
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` `2015` FALSE `saw it` `parent` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 34: a person of normal fortitude.
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` `2015` TRUE `saw it` `parent` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT shock `motor` `2015` TRUE `not there` `parent` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT shock `motor` `2015` TRUE `not there` `stranger` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT shock `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) TRUE `not there` `stranger` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

`consequential` MEANS `Can I recover economic loss for consequential mental harm`
#ASSERT consequential `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT consequential `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT consequential `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT consequential `work injury` `2015` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 8A -- good samaritans`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; individual, no reward; ill, injured or at risk; good faith, not reckless; at the scene or
-- by phone; before helping; impaired and careless; impersonating.
`samaritan` MEANS `Can I hold the good samaritan liable`
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 35B(4): the act came before helping (for example, causing the accident).
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` (d 21 10 2008) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT samaritan `ordinary` (d 22 10 2008) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT samaritan `motor` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 8B -- food donors`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; good faith, charitable, free; safe when it left; needed handling; told handling; time
-- limited; told time.
`food` MEANS `Can I hold the food donor liable`
#ASSERT food `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT food `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT food `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT food `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT food `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT food `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 9 -- public and other authorities`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; public authority; recreational; incapable; warned me; warned carer or parent; given or
-- adopted; safety law breach; contradicted; required; reckless.
`warning` MEANS `Did the authority owe me a duty despite its risk warning`
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An incapable person: only a warning to the carer or a parent counts (s 39(2)).
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT warning `motor` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; statutory duty claim; so unreasonable; regulate claim; could have compelled.
`statutory` MEANS `Can I hold the authority liable for breach of statutory duty or failure to regulate`
#ASSERT statutory `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT statutory `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT statutory `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT statutory `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Both kinds: s 40(3), s 41 applies in addition.
#ASSERT statutory `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT statutory `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT statutory `motor` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

`road` MEANS `Can I hold the road authority liable`
#ASSERT road `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT road `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT road `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A Part III motor accident injury: Part 9 is not kept (s 3B(2)), so s 42 does not protect the road authority.
#ASSERT road `motor` `2015` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 9A -- proportionate liability`

`econ` MEANS `economic loss or property damage from a failure to take reasonable care, not arising from personal injury`
`acl` MEANS `economic loss or property damage under the Australian Consumer Law (Tasmania) for a contravention of s 236`
`other claim` MEANS `a claim arising out of personal injury, or another claim`

`share` MEANS `How much can I recover from this concurrent wrongdoer`
#ASSERT share `ordinary` `2015` `econ` FALSE 500000 40 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT share `ordinary` `2015` `acl` FALSE 90000 30 EQUALS JUST 27000
#ASSERT share `ordinary` `2015` `econ` TRUE 500000 40 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT share `ordinary` `2015` `other claim` FALSE 500000 40 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT share `ordinary` (d 31 5 2005) `econ` FALSE 500000 40 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT share `ordinary` (d 1 6 2005) `econ` FALSE 500000 40 EQUALS JUST 200000

`more` MEANS `How much more can I recover from another wrongdoer`
#ASSERT more 500000 200000 300000 EQUALS 300000
#ASSERT more 500000 200000 350000 EQUALS 300000
#ASSERT more 500000 200000 100000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT more 500000 500000 100000 EQUALS 0

§§ `Part 10 -- volunteers`

`protected` MEANS `the volunteer is not liable; the community organisation that principally organised the work takes on the liability (ss 47(1), 48(1))`
`unprotected` MEANS `Part 10 does not protect the volunteer`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; community work; unpaid; court order; worker; good faith; defamation or insured vehicle;
-- outside scope; impaired.
`volunteer` MEANS `Can I hold the volunteer liable`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `protected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT volunteer `motor` `2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`

§§ `Part 10A -- accommodation providers`

-- Arguments: guest; negligence of provider or staff; deposited; sealed if asked; lost while deposited; notice shown.
`hotel` MEANS `Must the accommodation provider compensate me`
#ASSERT hotel TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT hotel TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT hotel TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT hotel TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT hotel TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 49A(3)(c): no notice displayed.
#ASSERT hotel TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT hotel FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 10B -- employer and employee`

`indemnify` MEANS `Must my employer indemnify me`
#ASSERT indemnify `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my employer must indemnify me, and I need not indemnify or contribute to my employer (s 49B(1))`
#ASSERT indemnify `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I need not indemnify or contribute to my employer; I am otherwise entitled to an indemnity (s 49B(1))`
#ASSERT indemnify `ordinary` `2015` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
#ASSERT indemnify `ordinary` `2015` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
#ASSERT indemnify `ordinary` `2015` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
#ASSERT indemnify `ordinary` (d 29 5 2012) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
#ASSERT indemnify `ordinary` (d 30 5 2012) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my employer must indemnify me, and I need not indemnify or contribute to my employer (s 49B(1))`
-- s 3B: Part 10B is not kept for a Part III motor accident injury, nor for child abuse; intentional harm and a workers
-- compensation Division 2 injury are out of the whole Act.
#ASSERT indemnify `motor` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
#ASSERT indemnify `intentional` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
#ASSERT indemnify `work injury` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
#ASSERT indemnify `child abuse` `2015` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 49B does not apply`
